{"ref": "HEADER", "text": "PROJECT: an Astro 7 static site (strict CSP: no inline script, no <style> block, no style attribute). The stylesheet already exists and owns every colour, size and movement. You write MARKUP ONLY, using exactly the class names listed below. Do not add classes that are not listed.\nIcons: <Icon name=\"...\"/> from '../components/Icon.astro'. Names that exist: menu, close, arrow, chat, pin, check (line) and whatsapp, instagram, facebook (brand). Never write svg.\nPlaceholders: a value in square brackets is a placeholder. Print it with set:html={ph(value)} where ph is imported from '../lib/ph' (it wraps the bracket text in a marked span). Never print a bracketed value as plain text.\nCopy rules: no em dashes, no serial comma, British English. Only use words given in this brief or read from the config.\n\nPART: src/components/Header.astro (frontmatter plus markup, nothing else).\nIMPORTS available: `import { site } from '../site.config';` `import { ph, waLink } from '../lib/ph';` `import Icon from './Icon.astro';`\nCONFIG you may read: site.name (string), site.nav (array of {href,label}), site.contact.whatsapp (digits), site.headerCta ({label,text}).\nIn the frontmatter define: const wa = waLink(site.contact.whatsapp, site.headerCta.text);\n\nMARKUP, in this order:\n<header class=\"site-header\">\n  <div class=\"site-header__bar gutter\">\n    <button class=\"site-header__menu\" type=\"button\" data-menu-toggle aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"site-menu\" aria-label=\"Open menu\"><Icon name=\"menu\" /><Icon name=\"close\" /></button>\n    <a class=\"brand\" href=\"/\"> holding <span set:html={ph(site.name)} />. Do NOT use id=\"top\" anywhere.\n    <nav class=\"site-nav\" id=\"site-menu\" aria-label=\"Main\"> with <ul class=\"site-nav__list\"> and one <li><a class=\"site-nav__link\" href={item.href}>{item.label}</a></li> per site.nav item (use .map).\n    <a class=\"site-header__cta\" href={wa} target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> containing <Icon name=\"chat\"/> then <span class=\"site-header__cta-label\">{site.headerCta.label}</span>\n  </div>\n</header>\nThe anchor with class brand must have a visible text child (the brand span). The cta anchor needs the label span so screen readers read it.\nCHECK (a machine runs this): the file contains the strings class=\"site-header\", class=\"site-header__bar gutter\", data-menu-toggle, aria-controls=\"site-menu\", id=\"site-menu\", site-nav__link, site-header__cta, waLink(, site.nav.map or site.nav.map(, <Icon name=\"menu\", <Icon name=\"close\", <Icon name=\"chat\"; it does NOT contain style=, <style, <script, id=\"top\", on[a-z]+=, an em dash, or the characters 'd=\"' (svg path data).\n"}
{"ref": "HERO", "text": "PROJECT: an Astro 7 static site (strict CSP: no inline script, no <style> block, no style attribute). The stylesheet already exists and owns every colour, size and movement. You write MARKUP ONLY, using exactly the class names listed below. Do not add classes that are not listed.\nIcons: <Icon name=\"...\"/> from '../components/Icon.astro'. Names that exist: menu, close, arrow, chat, pin, check (line) and whatsapp, instagram, facebook (brand). Never write svg.\nPlaceholders: a value in square brackets is a placeholder. Print it with set:html={ph(value)} where ph is imported from '../lib/ph' (it wraps the bracket text in a marked span). Never print a bracketed value as plain text.\nCopy rules: no em dashes, no serial comma, British English. Only use words given in this brief or read from the config.\n\nPART: src/components/Hero.astro (frontmatter plus markup, nothing else).\nIMPORTS available: `import { hero } from '../site.config';` `import { ph } from '../lib/ph';` `import Icon from './Icon.astro';` `import Picture from './Picture.astro';`\nCONFIG you may read: hero.lede (string), hero.piece.name, hero.piece.eyebrow, hero.piece.price (all placeholder strings in brackets), hero.doors.ready {label,href}, hero.doors.build {label,href}, hero.steps (array of {n,label,slot,alt}, four items, in the order 01 Timber, 02 Joined, 03 Finished, 04 At home).\nPicture takes props slot, alt and eager (boolean): <Picture slot={s.slot} alt={s.alt} eager={s.n === '03'} />\n\nSTORY: raw timber, then the joined frame, then the finished piece, then the piece at home. Four pictures stacked in one frame; the stylesheet fades them in as the page scrolls.\n\nMARKUP, in this exact structure and order:\n<section class=\"hero\" data-hero aria-labelledby=\"hero-title\">\n  <div class=\"hero__track\">\n    <div class=\"hero__stage gutter\">\n      <div class=\"hero__copy\">\n        <p class=\"hero__eyebrow\" set:html={ph(hero.piece.eyebrow)} />\n        <h1 class=\"hero__name\" id=\"hero-title\" set:html={ph(hero.piece.name)} />\n        <p class=\"hero__lede\">{hero.lede}</p>\n        <div class=\"hero__doors\">\n          <a class=\"btn btn--solid\" href={hero.doors.ready.href}>{hero.doors.ready.label} <span aria-hidden=\"true\">\u00b7</span> from <span set:html={ph(hero.piece.price)} /></a>\n          <a class=\"btn btn--line\" href={hero.doors.build.href}>{hero.doors.build.label} <Icon name=\"arrow\" /></a>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"hero__media\">\n        one <figure class=\"hero__frame\" data-step={index + 1}> per hero.steps item (use .map with the index), in array order, each holding the Picture.\n      </div>\n      <ol class=\"hero__steps\" aria-label=\"How a piece is made\">\n        one <li class=\"hero__step\" data-step={index + 1}><b>{s.n}</b><span>{s.label}</span></li> per hero.steps item.\n      </ol>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\nImportant: data-step values are the numbers 1 to 4 (index + 1), not the labels. Do NOT put id=\"top\" anywhere. Do not add any wrapper not listed.\nCHECK (a machine runs this): the file contains class=\"hero\", data-hero, class=\"hero__track\", class=\"hero__stage gutter\", class=\"hero__copy\", class=\"hero__eyebrow\", class=\"hero__name\", id=\"hero-title\", class=\"hero__lede\", class=\"hero__doors\", btn btn--solid, btn btn--line, class=\"hero__media\", class=\"hero__frame\", class=\"hero__steps\", class=\"hero__step\", hero.steps.map (twice), <Picture, <Icon name=\"arrow\", set:html={ph(hero.piece.name)}, set:html={ph(hero.piece.price)}; it does NOT contain style=, <style, <script, id=\"top\", on[a-z]+=, an em dash, or the characters 'd=\"'.\n"}
